WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.530 --> 00:00:06.819
The latest Disney and Pixar film to hit Disney+
is here just in time for summer — and it's

00:00:06.819 --> 00:00:08.700
certainly made a splash.

00:00:08.700 --> 00:00:14.049
The heartwarming animated feature "Luca,"
which arrived on Disney+ on June 18, is about

00:00:14.049 --> 00:00:17.410
a young sea monster's journey of self-discovery.

00:00:17.410 --> 00:00:19.840
Luca is a sheltered young goatfish herder.

00:00:19.840 --> 00:00:25.160
When he meets the brave Alberto, he realizes
that sea monsters turn into humans on land

00:00:25.160 --> 00:00:28.450
— and soon, he has a whole new world to
discover.

00:00:28.450 --> 00:00:34.410
The fun continues when Luca and Alberto meet
the feisty human girl Giulia in her seaside

00:00:34.410 --> 00:00:40.179
town of Portorosso, and the trio decide to
enter a triathlon together — all while Luca

00:00:40.179 --> 00:00:42.859
and Alberto try to hide their true identities.

00:00:42.859 --> 00:00:48.589
"Luca" is sure to be a hit with audiences
of all ages, thanks to its beautiful animation

00:00:48.589 --> 00:00:50.069
and touching story.

00:00:50.069 --> 00:00:54.949
While the plot of "Luca" has the same happy,
upbeat tone and structure characteristic of

00:00:54.949 --> 00:01:00.280
Disney-Pixar movies, there are plenty of unique
aspects to "Luca" that make it a film unlike

00:01:00.280 --> 00:01:01.280
any other.

00:01:01.280 --> 00:01:04.409
Here's what happens at the end of "Luca,"
and what it means.

00:01:04.409 --> 00:01:05.659
Spoilers ahead!

00:01:05.659 --> 00:01:10.060
The final scenes of "Luca" have the potential
to leave viewers with a bunch of unanswered

00:01:10.060 --> 00:01:11.060
questions.

00:01:11.060 --> 00:01:16.070
In the film's last moments, Luca heads off
to join Giulia at her school, leaving Alberto

00:01:16.070 --> 00:01:19.570
behind with Giulia's kind father Massimo.

00:01:19.570 --> 00:01:21.310
Bittersweet ending, right?

00:01:21.310 --> 00:01:25.860
It also leaves some loose ends: Will Luca
be accepted at his school in the human world?

00:01:25.860 --> 00:01:27.869
What will become of Alberto?

00:01:27.869 --> 00:01:32.670
Thankfully, the filmmakers address these concerns
-- though you have to stick around for the

00:01:32.670 --> 00:01:33.670
end credits.

00:01:33.670 --> 00:01:38.140
As the credits roll, sketches show that the
two boys are staying in touch, and they're

00:01:38.140 --> 00:01:40.149
all enjoying their new lives.

00:01:40.149 --> 00:01:44.539
The themes of friendship and acceptance also
have a big role to play in the ending.

00:01:44.539 --> 00:01:49.920
Though Luca, Alberto, and Giulia have their
ups and downs throughout the film, they ultimately

00:01:49.920 --> 00:01:54.409
prove to be genuine friends who care about
and support each other for who they are.

00:01:54.409 --> 00:01:59.909
This is especially evident when Giulia realizes
that Luca and Alberto are sea monsters.

00:01:59.909 --> 00:02:04.540
She's a bit surprised at first, but quickly
accepts their true nature and concerns herself

00:02:04.540 --> 00:02:06.719
with making sure they stay safe.

00:02:06.719 --> 00:02:11.370
Since Giulia is a bit of an outcast herself,
it's especially touching to see how easy it

00:02:11.370 --> 00:02:16.300
is for her to accept her friends, knowing
that she isn't always so readily accepted.

00:02:16.300 --> 00:02:21.530
The close and quick bond that Luca and Alberto
share is even more special when you realize

00:02:21.530 --> 00:02:26.519
it was inspired by "Luca" director Enrico
Casarosa's real childhood.

00:02:26.519 --> 00:02:27.819
He told Disney News:

00:02:27.819 --> 00:02:33.100
"My best friend Alberto was a bit of a troublemaker,
[while] I was very timid and had a bit of

00:02:33.100 --> 00:02:36.459
a sheltered life — we couldn't have been
more different.

00:02:36.459 --> 00:02:40.909
[...] Alberto pushed me out of my comfort
zone, and pushed me off many cliffs, metaphorically

00:02:40.909 --> 00:02:41.909
and not.

00:02:41.909 --> 00:02:46.239
I probably would not be here if I didn't learn
to chase my dreams from him."

00:02:46.239 --> 00:02:47.920
That thread runs throughout the movie.

00:02:47.920 --> 00:02:52.420
"Luca" constantly reminds us to be proud of
who we are and accept others as they are as

00:02:52.420 --> 00:02:53.420
well.

00:02:53.420 --> 00:02:57.170
None of the friends in "Luca" try to change
one another — instead, they encourage each

00:02:57.170 --> 00:02:59.959
other to be themselves, as good friends should.

00:02:59.959 --> 00:03:04.340
A short scene with Massimo is another great
example of acceptance.

00:03:04.340 --> 00:03:09.159
When he catches Alberto staring at his missing
arm, he jokes that a sea monster ate it before

00:03:09.159 --> 00:03:12.290
explaining that it's simply how he came into
the world.

00:03:12.290 --> 00:03:16.040
The topic isn't brought up again, and the
moment serves as a reminder that someone's

00:03:16.040 --> 00:03:18.959
differences aren't the most important parts
of them.

00:03:18.959 --> 00:03:23.680
Instead, Massimo's kindness, fishing skills,
and love for his daughter are the focus of

00:03:23.680 --> 00:03:24.959
his character.

00:03:24.959 --> 00:03:29.400
Andrea Warren, the producer of "Luca," expanded
on the film's theme of acceptance.

00:03:29.400 --> 00:03:30.750
She told Disney News:

00:03:30.750 --> 00:03:35.450
"We always liked the idea that the metaphor
of being a sea monster can apply to so many

00:03:35.450 --> 00:03:36.650
different things.

00:03:36.650 --> 00:03:42.000
There is a theme of openness, showing oneself
and self-acceptance, as well as community

00:03:42.000 --> 00:03:43.000
acceptance.

00:03:43.000 --> 00:03:44.000
"

00:03:44.000 --> 00:03:47.260
"And I hope that really, yeah, makes us think
about the friendships that have helped us

00:03:47.260 --> 00:03:48.519
find ourselves."

00:03:48.519 --> 00:03:53.219
The ending of "Luca" shows how these friendships
forged during childhood -- sometimes even

00:03:53.219 --> 00:03:57.680
over just one fateful summer -- have the power
to define us long after.

00:03:57.680 --> 00:04:02.530
Thanks to Giulia's acceptance of him and Alberto's
constant urging to step outside his comfort

00:04:02.530 --> 00:04:07.480
zone, Luca learns to embrace all the opportunities
life presents him.

